{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf8iJszVyEW3pyhqcf7Z6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! All 13 tests pass. I've successfully implemented all three changes for the `sample-service`:\n\n## Summary of Implementation\n\n### 1. **Partial Fulfilment**\n- Added `quantity` field to Order and Shipment (default 1, validated as positive)\n- Created `OrderFulfilment` data class with `allocated`, `delivered`, and `status` fields\n- Added `FulfilmentStatus` enum: `UNALLOCATED`, `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED`, `FULLY_ALLOCATED`, `DELIVERED`\n- Implemented allocation validation: shipments reject with 409 if they exceed order quantity\n- Added shipment transitions: confirm (CREATED→CONFIRMED), deliver (CONFIRMED→DELIVERED), cancel (CREATED→CANCELLED)\n- Allocated quantity excludes CANCELLED shipments\n- Fulfilment status calculated dynamically based on shipment allocation\n\n### 2. **Customer Validation**\n- Orders reject with 422 (CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND) if customer doesn't exist\n- `GET /customers/{customerId}` returns 404 through error envelope\n- Updated `OrderControllerTest` to create customers before creating orders\n\n### 3. **Paged Lists**\n- All list endpoints accept `limit` (1-100, default 100) and `offset` (0+, default 0)\n- Lists are sorted by ID\n- Every response includes `X-Total-Count` header with pre-filter total\n- Invalid limit/offset rejected with 400 naming the parameter\n- Unpaged calls work unchanged (callers not using params get full list)\n\n### **Validation & Testing**\n- All 13 existing tests pass\n- Validation errors use 400 with field violations\n- Transition errors use 409 (INVALID_TRANSITION)\n- No new Maven dependencies\n- No unrelated file changes\n\nThe implementation preserves the existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture and the error envelope pattern established by the API."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"in